%% DM26-0670

%% A person's certificate from an identity provider's token. Built, tested, and refused where it runs today: nothing renders CREDENTIALS_AGENT_INTROSPECTION_*, so an IdP token
%% stops at the introspection with TokenIntrospectionFailed. How people get certificates today is general/admin_bootstrap_identity, an account provisioned and claimed, with no IdP
%% and no grant. Shaded: designed and not built. Checked against the code 2026-11-04, not run against an IdP.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User as End user
    participant UserTool as user-cert-fetcher
    participant IdP as Identity provider
    participant Obs as Credentials observer<br/>(low trust)
    participant Bk as Cassini broker
    participant Con as Credentials agent<br/>(consumer)
    participant Ledger as Ledger
    participant CI as cert-issuer
    participant App as A Polar app

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over User,IdP: DESIGNED: the tool takes the user through the IdP.<br/>Today it reads a token from --credential-path, and getting one is the user's business
    UserTool->>IdP: Authorization Code flow
    IdP-->>UserTool: an access token
    end

    User->>UserTool: run it, with the token in a file
    UserTool->>Obs: POST /identity, as in identity_normalization_query
    Obs-->>UserTool: the normalized identity
    UserTool->>UserTool: make a key here, which never leaves, and a CSR naming that identity
    UserTool->>Obs: POST /issue { csr_pem, credential, cert_type, names }
    Obs->>Obs: parse the CSR, 400 if it does not. No trust decision
    Obs-)Bk: credentials-issuance-requests, with a fresh correlation id
    Bk-)Con: delivered, through the request gate, judged as the observer

    Con->>Con: classify the credential, check the request's shape
    Con->>IdP: for an IdP token, RFC 7662 introspection: signature alone cannot see a session ended early.<br/>No introspection client configured is a refusal
    IdP-->>Con: still valid, or not
    Con->>CI: POST /validate, asking for the normalized identity
    CI-->>Con: the identity, and any instance binding
    Con->>Ledger: CheckGrant by the token's identity
    Note over Con,Ledger: A grant adds p: names to a client certificate. Required for an IdP token. None: NoGrantFound
    Con->>Con: for a Kubernetes credential only, the instance check
    Con->>Ledger: Admit: this identity, instance and type, not within five minutes. Else TooSoon, 429
    Con->>CI: POST /issue, with the grant's names
    alt it signs
        CI-->>Con: the certificate
        Con->>Ledger: append IssuanceCompleted, synced before the fold. A client certificate uses up its grant
        Ledger--)Con: the projection is told, fire and forget (graph_projection_catch_up)
    else it does not
        Con->>Ledger: release the admission
    end

    Con-)Bk: Issued { certificate, chain, escrow public key }, or Refused, on credentials-issuance-replies
    Bk-)Obs: the reply, by correlation id
    Obs-->>UserTool: the certificate, or the status for the refusal
    UserTool->>UserTool: write them to --cert-dir. It ignores the escrow key, and imports nothing into a browser

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over User,App: DESIGNED: downstream use
    User->>App: mTLS, with the installed certificate
    App->>App: identity and permissions read<br/>from the certificate's names, with no<br/>call to the IdP, Cassini or Neo4j
    App-->>User: session established
    end
